# Selector Library Quick Reference

> **Full documentation**: See [docs/selectors-and-testids.md](../docs/selectors-and-testids.md)
> · **Syntax and traps**: [symbolic-selector-syntax.md](skills/convert-guide-selectors/symbolic-selector-syntax.md)
> · **Converting a guide**: the `convert-guide-selectors` skill

## Selector Priority

1. **Symbolic `grafana:` references** -- resolve through `@grafana/e2e-selectors` per Grafana version
2. `data-testid` attributes -- stable, but pinned to one version's value
3. Semantic attributes: `href`, `aria-*`, `id`, `role`
4. `:contains()` text matching -- matches **translated** copy; breaks in any non-English UI
5. `:has()` structural matching (match by descendants)
6. **Avoid**: Auto-generated CSS classes like `.css-8mjxyo`

## Symbolic References (Preferred)

A `grafana:` reftarget resolves through `@grafana/e2e-selectors` against the **running** Grafana version and matches `data-testid` **or** `aria-label`. A literal `data-testid` is a snapshot of one version's value in one attribute.

| Form | Use for | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| `grafana:<path>` | the whole reftarget | `grafana:components.TimePicker.openButton` |
| `grafana:<path>:<arg>` | parameterized selectors | `grafana:components.Tab.title:Related metrics` |
| `{grafana:<path>}` | inside a larger CSS expression | `a{grafana:components.Tab.title:Winner}` |

`<path>` is a dotted path into the package's `components` or `pages` exports. Verify every path before shipping -- one unresolvable token voids the whole reftarget:

```bash
GRAFANA_REPO=~/Repos/grafana npx tsx skills/convert-guide-selectors/scripts/validate-paths.ts \
  '["components.TimePicker.openButton"]' "12.4.0,13.2.0"
```

**Only reference selectors that exist in a shipped release.** A selector newly merged to grafana/grafana resolves to nothing on the instances your guide runs against today.

## Navigation Selectors

Nav menu **items** are the one documented exception -- they stay literal. Pathfinder regex-matches this exact shape to auto-expand a collapsed menu section, and a resolved reference defeats that fix. The `[href]` discriminator isn't in the selector package anyway.

```
Home:        a[data-testid='data-testid Nav menu item'][href='/']
Dashboards:  a[data-testid='data-testid Nav menu item'][href='/dashboards']
Explore:     a[data-testid='data-testid Nav menu item'][href='/explore']
Alerting:    a[data-testid='data-testid Nav menu item'][href='/alerting']
Connections: a[data-testid='data-testid Nav menu item'][href='/connections']
Admin:       a[data-testid='data-testid Nav menu item'][href='/admin']
```

The surrounding container has no such constraint: `{grafana:components.NavMenu.Menu}`.

## Button by Text

`action: "button"` is the most readable option when nothing better exists, but it is a **text match** -- it compares against translated copy exactly as `:contains()` does, so it works in English and silently matches nothing in every other locale.

Where a `grafana:` reference or a `data-testid` exists for the button, use that instead. Where none does, that's a gap to fix in grafana/grafana rather than paper over here.

```json
{ "action": "button", "reftarget": "Save & test" }
{ "action": "button", "reftarget": "Add new data source" }
{ "action": "button", "reftarget": "New" }
```

## Form Elements

No package selectors for these; `id` is already version-independent.

```
Data source name:  input[id='basic-settings-name']
Connection URL:    input[id='connection-url']
Query editor:      textarea.inputarea.monaco-mouse-cursor-text
```

## Advanced Selectors

### `panel:<title>` - Scope into a panel
```json
"reftarget": "panel:CPU Usage > div[data-testid='uplot-main-div']"
```
Expands to `[data-viz-panel-key]:has([data-testid*="Panel header <title>"]) <rest>`. The separator must be exactly `" > "`, spaces included, and joins with a **descendant** combinator despite the `>`.

> ⚠️ **`panel:` and `{grafana:}` are mutually exclusive.** The resolver dispatches on `{grafana:` **first** and returns immediately, so a reftarget containing both never reaches the `panel:` branch -- `panel:CPU > {grafana:…}` resolves the token and leaves the literal text `panel:CPU > ` in front of it, matching nothing. Pick one:
>
> ```json
> // panel: shorthand -- the tail stays plain CSS
> "reftarget": "panel:CPU Usage > div[data-testid='uplot-main-div']"
>
> // fully symbolic -- both halves version-aware, no panel: prefix
> "reftarget": "section{grafana:components.Panels.Panel.title:CPU Usage} {grafana:components.UPlotChart.container}"
> ```

### `:has(selector)` - Parent with child
```json
"reftarget": "div[data-cy='item']:has(p:contains('service'))"
```

### `:contains('text')` - By text content
```json
"reftarget": "div:contains('checkoutservice')"
```
Matches translated copy -- see Selector Priority above.

### `:nth-match(n)` - Global nth element
```json
"reftarget": "div[data-testid='panel']:nth-match(3)"
```
**Last resort.** The index counts what is *currently rendered*, and Grafana lazy-renders panels and virtualizes long lists, so `n` shifts as the user scrolls. Scope to a container (`panel:<title> > ...`, or a row-scoped selector) instead. See [dashboard-selector-strategies.md](skills/autogen-guide-dashboard/dashboard-selector-strategies.md).

## Drilldown Selectors

```
Metrics drilldown app: a[data-testid='data-testid Nav menu item'][href='/a/grafana-metricsdrilldown-app/drilldown']
Select metric action:  button[data-testid^="select-action_"]
Related metrics tab:   grafana:components.Tab.title:Related metrics
Related logs tab:      grafana:components.Tab.title:Related logs
```

The drilldown app entrypoint is a nav item, so it stays literal. `select-action_` is a plugin test id with a metric-name suffix -- match the prefix with `^=` rather than pinning one metric.

## Hover-Dependent UI

**Show mode**: highlights element without triggering hover events.
**Do mode**: dispatches mouseenter/mouseover/mousemove, triggers CSS `:hover` states. Maintains hover for 2 seconds.

Use multistep or guided:
```json
{
  "type": "multistep",
  "steps": [
    { "action": "hover", "reftarget": "tr[data-row-id='123']" },
    { "action": "button", "reftarget": "Edit" }
  ]
}
```

## Lazy-Rendered Containers

Virtualized tables, paginated lists, and dashboard rows below the fold do not render off-screen elements. Set `lazyRender: true` on the step (and optionally `scrollContainer` — default `.scrollbar-view`) to scroll the target into view first. Use a `guided` block, not plain `interactive` — user-paced detection avoids racing the scroll. See [docs/json-guide-reference.md — Step Structure](../docs/json-guide-reference.md#step-structure).

## Performance Tips

- Engine tries native `querySelector()` first, falls back to JS parsing
- Use specific base selectors to narrow scope
- **Prefer attribute matching over text or structure** -- a `grafana:` reference or a `data-testid` resolves to a single attribute lookup, while `:contains()` and `:has()` fall back to walking the DOM in JS. A reference costs one extra map lookup at resolve time and is the most *stable* option; a literal `data-testid` is marginally faster and pins one version
- Test in target browsers when using `:has()` on older Firefox
- For virtualized targets, set `lazyRender: true` so the engine scrolls them into view
